  "pulses_h2_1f_note": "Effect of each C-segment pulse in 1F f_main (runs/20261023T075845Z_s1f_s2), truth, from the pulse command to the next look (settle_s standing + 5 frames), robot frame before the pulse: [mean, sd] over n. These pulses come one after another with only 1.0 s of standing between them, and they differ from the single pulses from a 3 s settled stand in pulses_mac: F2 goes 3.8 cm (not 2.1) and forward pulses turn right on average (F2 -2.9, F5 -2.2 deg, not +4.9 and +4.2) with a much wider spread (F5 sd 8.0 deg, -21 to +27). The robot was standing still before each pulse (trunk speed < 0.01 m/s), so this is the gait starting from wherever the feet ended, not leftover motion. R17 and B10 were too rare in 1F and are copied from pulses_mac. The C segment uses this table (stage1.json inching.pulse_table).",
